// `hw.os` lists what it runs (pi-os, pi-os-cm, debian-arm64, debian-amd64,
// windows…) and `hw.sdrCh` the work it can do, in a way the sums can use: 8
// times its speed as a whole computer in Raspberry Pi 4s (a Pi 4 is 8, a
// Pi 3B+ 4, an N150 24). The hardware review (docs/hardware-review/research/R8
// and the lead reviewer's planning values) sets each one from published
// benchmarks of the same processor, because nobody has run RPi ALERT's decoder
// on any computer but a Pi 4: every figure but the Pi 4's is a stand-in, and
// conf is 'low' where the speed is a guess. A channel is decoded on ONE core,
// so `hw.cores` (or the processor text) says how many cores share that work: a
// core's speed is sdrCh ÷ 2 ÷ cores, in Pi 4 cores. Also recorded where the
// reports give them, for comparison tables: `hw.tpm`, `hw.secureBoot`,
// `hw.fanless` (true or false) and `hw.dcIn` (free text; the item dialog does
